' 20 PathMap re-rooting: R(s, v), the delivery of one argument on a prefix.
'
' Source of Figure N11.7b in ../design.md (section N11.7). The figure restates
' reroot of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/pathmap/reroot.rs and the
' adapter of pathmap/adapter.rs (P5e). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The suffix s is the part of the send path p after the prefix q.
'   2. An empty suffix delivers the value as it is.
'   3. A PathMap value gets the suffix in front of each entry, and an empty
'      PathMap becomes the unit {| s |}.
'   4. Every other value becomes the list of the suffix and the value.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 20-pathmap-reroot.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 20-pathmap-reroot
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
title <latex>R(s, v)</latex>: the delivery of one argument on the prefix q

start
:the argument v of a datum on the path p; <<$rrs_object>>
:the suffix <latex>s = p \setminus q</latex>; <<$rrs_object>>
if (s is empty?) then (yes)
  :deliver v as it is; <<$rrs_effect>>
elseif (v is one EPathMap?) then (yes)
  :decode v with the adapter
  (paths in key order, one path for each key); <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (the map has no entry?) then (yes)
    :deliver the unit <latex>\{| s |\}</latex>; <<$rrs_effect>>
  else (no)
    :deliver <latex>\{| s \mathbin{+\!\!+} \mathrm{elems}(e) |\}</latex>
    for each entry e; <<$rrs_effect>>
  endif
  :encode the map with the adapter
  (the canonical entry form); <<$rrs_agent>>
else (no)
  :deliver the list <latex>[s_1, \ldots, s_k, v]</latex>; <<$rrs_effect>>
endif
stop
@enduml
